IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- THE RADIO-COMMUNICATION REGULATIONS AS MADE, AND THEIR 2001 AMENDMENTS (deposited 2026-11-04 from the e-Gazette's third list of exact URLs).
-- Telecommunications (Radio-communication) Regulations 2001, S 114/2001 (first published 2 March 2001 at 5:00 pm, in operation 2 March 2001), are the Rg 5 before its 2002 Revised Edition
-- (TA1999-RG5.txt, history line "[G.N. Nos. S114/2001; S 374/2001; S 450/2001]").  Four amendments of 2001 follow:
--   S 339/2001  first published 9 Jul 2001, in operation 9 Jul 2001: inserts Part II item 11, "Fixed Wireless Broadband Network, $500 per group of 50 stations or part thereof".
--   S 373/2001  a Corrigendum, first published 1 Aug 2001: S 339/2001 "which have been published in error are to be treated as cancelled".
--   S 374/2001  first published 1 Aug 2001, "deemed to have come into operation on 9th July 2001": the same insertion, made by the Info-communications Development Authority of Singapore
--               (S 339/2001 was made by the Minister).
--   S 450/2001  "Amendment No. 2", first published 18 Sep 2001, in operation 18 Sep 2001: substitutes reg 26(4), adds reg 28(1)(d) "Fixed Wireless Network Licence", deletes "Broadband" in Part I item 4
--               and Part II item 11 and "Ground" in Part II item 7(c) of the First Schedule, and inserts Part II item 12, "Special Purpose Station, $50".
-- WHAT THIS MODULE ENCODES.  (1) A table of how each regulation of S 114/2001 compares, word for word, with the 2002 Revised Edition deposited as TA1999-RG5.txt (the comparison is by script,
-- after setting aside case, punctuation other than the parentheses of paragraph labels, hyphenation and page furniture; 59 of the 80 regulations are the same words, and for each of the other 21 the difference is
-- stated).  Where the words are the same, the encoded rule of the Revised Edition is the as-made rule; where they differ, the rule is NOT carried back (its function answers NOTHING before 1 Jan 2003).
-- (2) The effect of the four amendments of 2001 on reg 26(4), reg 28(1) and the First Schedule's category names, as functions of both days.
-- The Revised Edition's own start day (1 Jan 2003) is assumed (NOTES.md Fork B); it prints the Regulations as made and as amended by S 374/2001 and S 450/2001.
-- The Schedules: the First Schedule's words differ from the Revised Edition's only in layout and in the 2001 amendments; the Second and Third Schedules are the same words.

§ `S 114/2001: the Regulations as made (in operation 2 March 2001)`

