-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:181 | The Schedules
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:185 | In exercise of the powers conferred by section 74 of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:186 | Telecommunications Act, the Info-communications Development
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:187 | Authority of Singapore, with the approval of the Minister for
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:188 | Communications and Information Technology, hereby makes the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:189 | following Regulations:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:191 | PART I
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:192 | PRELIMINARY
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:194 | Citation and commencement
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:195 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:196 | (Radio-communication) Regulations 2001 and shall come into
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:197 | operation on 2nd March 2001.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:199 | Definitions
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:200 | 2. In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:201 | ‘‘Amateur Station’’ means a station in respect of which an
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:202 | Amateur Station licensee is authorised in the licence to use;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:203 | ‘‘armed forces’’ means the Singapore Armed Forces established
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:204 | under the Singapore Armed Forces Act (Cap. 295) and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:205 | includes any visiting force, not being a police force, which is
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:206 | lawfully present in Singapore;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:209 | ‘‘Armed Forces Communication’’ means radio-communication —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:210 | (a) between stations of the armed forces; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:211 | (b) between stations of the armed forces and any other
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:212 | radio-communication station, whether on shore or on
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:213 | any vessel or aircraft;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:214 | ‘‘authorised officer’’ means any officer authorised by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:215 | Authority to act on its behalf;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:216 | ‘‘class licence’’ means a class licence referred to in regulation 65;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:217 | ‘‘class licensee’’ means a person who is deemed to have been
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:218 | granted a class licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:219 | ‘‘interference’’ —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:220 | (a) in relation to radio-communication, means interference
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:221 | to or with radio-communications that is attributable,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:222 | whether wholly or partly and whether directly or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:223 | indirectly, to an emission of electromagnetic energy by
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:224 | any device; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:225 | (b) in relation to the uses or functions of any station,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:226 | network or radio-communication equipment, means
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:227 | interference to or with the uses or functions that is
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:228 | attributable, whether wholly or partly and whether
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:229 | directly or indirectly, to an emission of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:230 | electromagnetic energy by the station, network or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:231 | radio-communication equipment;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:232 | ‘‘International Telecommunication Convention’’ means the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:233 | Convention of the International Telecommunication Union
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:234 | signed at Nairobi in 1982 or any subsequent revision or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:235 | modification thereof to which the Government of Singapore
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:236 | is a party;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:237 | ‘‘licence’’ means a station (spectrum) licence, a network
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:238 | (spectrum) licence, a station licence, a network licence or a
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:239 | class licence or all or any of these licences, as the context may
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:240 | require;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:241 | ‘‘licensee’’ —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:242 | (a) in relation to a station (spectrum) licence, a network
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:243 | (spectrum) licence, a station licence or a network
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:244 | licence, means the holder of the licence; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:247 | (b) in relation to a class licence, means the person deemed
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:248 | to have been granted the class licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:249 | ‘‘localised private network’’ means a private network that
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:250 | provides radio coverage of a confined or restricted area as
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:251 | specified by the Authority and that comprises at least 2
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:252 | stations each operating generally at an effective radiated
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:253 | power of 5 watts or below;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:254 | ‘‘Localised Radio-communication Station’’ means a station that
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:255 | can only be used for communication with a base station or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:256 | with another station within a defined power limit specified by
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:257 | the Authority;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:258 | ‘‘network’’ means 2 or more stations operated by a person and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:259 | used or intended to be used in communication with one
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:260 | another;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:261 | ‘‘network licence’’ means a licence referred to in regulation 28;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:262 | ‘‘network (spectrum) licence’’ means a licence referred to in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:263 | regulation 23;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:264 | ‘‘private network’’ means a network which —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:265 | (a) exists to meet the exclusive internal
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:266 | telecommunication needs of the licensee; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:267 | (b) has a number of common interest groups of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:268 | subscribers or users and radio channels as the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:269 | Authority may specify;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:270 | ‘‘public mobile network’’ means any public network that
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:271 | enables radio-communications through the use of portable
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:272 | or mobile stations and may include any of the following
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:273 | telecommunication systems licensed under section 5 of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:274 | Act:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:275 | (a) a public cellular mobile telephone system;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:276 | (b) a public radio paging system;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:277 | (c) a public mobile data system;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:278 | (d) a public trunked radio system; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:279 | (e) a public satellite mobile telephone or data system;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:282 | ‘‘public network’’ means a network which is accessible to any
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:283 | member of the public generally and which is used or intended
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:284 | to be used to provide telecommunication services by means
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:285 | of radio-communication to the general public;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:286 | ‘‘radio frequency band’’ means any contiguous range of radio
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:287 | frequencies;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:288 | ‘‘radio frequency band plan’’ means a plan prepared under
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:289 | regulation 4;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:290 | ‘‘radio frequency spectrum’’ means the range of frequencies
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:291 | within which radio-communications are capable of being
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:292 | made;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:293 | ‘‘Radio Regulations’’ means the Radio Regulations annexed to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:294 | the International Telecommunication Convention and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:295 | includes every revision or modification thereof which the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:296 | Government has ratified or accepted;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:297 | ‘‘radio spectrum plan’’ means a plan prepared under regulation 3;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:298 | ‘‘reception’’, in relation to any radio emission, includes
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:299 | interception;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:300 | ‘‘spectrum right’’ means a right to use any specified part of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:301 | radio frequency spectrum granted under regulation 6 (2);
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:302 | ‘‘station’’ means a transmitter, a receiver, a combination of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:303 | transmitters and receivers or any accessory thereto which is
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:304 | used or intended to be used for radio-communication;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:305 | ‘‘station licence’’ means a Ship Station Licence, an Aircraft Station
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:306 | Licence, an Amateur Station Licence, an Experimental Station
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:307 | Licence, a Localised Radio-communication Station Licence,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:308 | a General Radio-communication Station Licence, a Satellite
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:309 | Communication Station Licence or a Special Purpose Station
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:310 | Licence, granted under Part VI;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:311 | ‘‘station (spectrum) licence’’ means a licence referred to in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:312 | regulation 23;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:313 | ‘‘wide-area private network’’ means a private network that
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:314 | provides radio coverage of a wide area as specified by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:315 | Authority and that comprises one or more stations
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:316 | operating generally at an effective radiated power of more
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:317 | than 5 watts.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:320 | PART II
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:321 | RADIO SPECTRUM PLAN AND
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:322 | RADIO FREQUENCY BAND PLAN
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:324 | Radio spectrum plans
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:325 | 3.—(1) The Authority may prepare and publish for information a
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:326 | radio spectrum plan in any form as it considers appropriate.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:327 | (2) A radio spectrum plan shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:328 | (a) conform with the Radio Regulations;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:329 | (b) have regard to any agreement, treaty or convention between
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:330 | Singapore and any other country, in relation to radio
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:331 | frequency band planning and radio emission;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:332 | (c) divide into such number of radio frequency bands as the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:333 | Authority considers appropriate so much of the radio
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:334 | spectrum as the Authority considers necessary for the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:335 | purpose of regulating radio-communication; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:336 | (d) specify the general purpose for which each radio frequency
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:337 | band may be used.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:339 | Radio frequency band plans
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:340 | 4.—(1) The Authority may prepare and publish for information a
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:341 | radio frequency band plan in any form as it considers appropriate
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:342 | relating to one or more radio frequency bands.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:343 | (2) A radio frequency band plan shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:344 | (a) be consistent with the use of the radio frequency bands
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:345 | specified in the radio spectrum plan;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:346 | (b) conform with any applicable radio frequency band allocation
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:347 | plans made pursuant to any agreement, treaty or convention
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:348 | which is binding on Singapore; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:349 | (c) specify the purpose for which the radio frequency band may
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:350 | be used.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:352 | Variation or revocation of radio spectrum plan and radio frequency
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:353 | band plan
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:354 | 5. The Authority may vary or revoke any radio spectrum plan or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:355 | radio frequency band plan, in whole or in part.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:358 | PART III
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:359 | SPECTRUM RIGHTS
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:360 | Division 1
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:361 | Allocation and Conditions of Spectrum Rights
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:363 | Allocation of spectrum rights
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:364 | 6.—(1) The Authority may determine that any specified part of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:365 | radio frequency spectrum shall be allocated for use by persons by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:366 | grant of spectrum rights, but subject to such restrictions as the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:367 | Authority considers appropriate.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:368 | (2) Subject to this Part, the Authority may, upon payment of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:369 | charges determined by the Authority, grant any person the right to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:370 | use any specified part of the radio frequency spectrum referred to in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:371 | paragraph (1) for such period as it may specify.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:373 | Procedures for determining allocation of spectrum rights
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:374 | 7. The procedure for allocating spectrum rights, the conditions for
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:375 | participation in the allocation of spectrum rights and the charges
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:376 | payable for spectrum rights shall be determined by the Authority and,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:377 | without limiting the methods which may be used, may include any
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:378 | one or a combination of the following methods:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:379 | (a) by auction;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:380 | (b) by tender; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:381 | (c) by allocation for a pre-determined fee or a negotiated fee.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:383 | Allocation of spectrum rights subject to requirements
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:384 | 8. The Authority may refuse to grant any spectrum right to any
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:385 | person unless the person meets such requirements as the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:386 | may determine.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:388 | Exclusion from allocation of spectrum rights
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:389 | 9.—(1) The Authority may, for the purpose of developing the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:390 | communications industry in Singapore and maintaining effective
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:391 | competition between persons engaged in the provision of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:392 | radio-communication services, or in the public interest, by notice in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:393 | writing, exclude any person from participating, or limit any person’s
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:394 | participation, in the allocation of any spectrum right.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:397 | (2) Before excluding any person from participating, or limiting any
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:398 | person’s participation, in the allocation of any spectrum right, the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:399 | Authority shall give the affected person an opportunity to be heard.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:400 | (3) Any person aggrieved by the Authority’s decision under this
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:401 | regulation to exclude any person from obtaining, or limit any person’s
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:402 | right to obtain, any spectrum right may appeal to the Minister whose
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:403 | decision shall be final.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:405 | Conditions of grant of spectrum rights
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:406 | 10. A spectrum right granted by the Authority shall be subject to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:407 | such conditions as the Authority considers appropriate, including —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:408 | (a) conditions specifying the part or parts of the radio frequency
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:409 | spectrum in which the operation of a station or network is
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:410 | authorised;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:411 | (b) conditions specifying the type of station or network, and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:412 | type of equipment comprising the station or network, which
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:413 | the person granted the spectrum right is authorised to operate;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:414 | (c) conditions specifying the periods during which operation of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:415 | a station or network is authorised;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:416 | (d) conditions specifying that the person granted the spectrum
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:417 | right and persons authorised by that person to operate a
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:418 | station or network shall not operate any station or network
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:419 | without a station (spectrum) licence or a network (spectrum)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:420 | licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:421 | (e) conditions specifying the maximum permitted level of radio
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:422 | emission, that may be caused by operation of a station or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:423 | network under the licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:424 | (f) conditions specifying the area within which operation of a
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:425 | station or network is authorised;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:426 | (g) conditions specifying the maximum permitted level of radio
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:427 | emission, outside the area referred to in paragraph (f), that
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:428 | may be caused by the operation of the station or network;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:429 | (h) conditions requiring the payment to the Authority of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:430 | charges for the spectrum right determined by the Authority;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:431 | (i) conditions requiring the person granted the spectrum right
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:432 | to comply with the directions of the Authority concerning
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:433 | the use of the spectrum right; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:434 | (j) such other conditions as the Authority considers appropriate.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:437 | Authorisation to use assigned part of radio frequency spectrum
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:438 | 11.—(1) Subject to paragraph (2), a spectrum right authorises —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:439 | (a) the person granted the spectrum right; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:440 | (b) if the conditions of the grant of spectrum right permit, any
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:441 | person authorised by the person granted the spectrum right,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:442 | to use the assigned radio frequency spectrum, in accordance with the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:443 | conditions of the grant, for the purpose of operating a station or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:444 | network.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:445 | (2) Except as may be permitted by the Authority, a person is not
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:446 | authorised to operate a station or network under paragraph (1) unless
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:447 | the person has, and complies with the conditions of, a station
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:448 | (spectrum) licence or a network (spectrum) licence, as the case may be.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:450 | Division 2
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:451 | Spectrum Sharing and Trading
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:453 | Spectrum sharing
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:454 | 12.—(1) Subject to such conditions as the Authority may generally
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:455 | or specifically impose, a person granted a spectrum right may
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:456 | authorise another person to use the assigned radio frequency
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:457 | spectrum, in accordance with the conditions of the grant, for the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:458 | purpose of operating a station or network subject to that person
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:459 | obtaining a station (spectrum) licence or a network (spectrum)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:460 | licence, as the case may be.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:461 | (2) Any person authorised by a person granted a spectrum right to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:462 | use the assigned radio frequency spectrum under paragraph (1) shall
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:463 | comply with the Act, these Regulations and such other requirements
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:464 | as the Authority may specify.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:466 | Spectrum trading
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:467 | 13.—(1) Subject to such conditions as the Authority may generally
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:468 | or specifically impose, a person granted a spectrum right may assign,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:469 | or otherwise deal with, the whole or any part of the rights and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:470 | privileges granted under the spectrum right.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:471 | (2) No assignment of or dealing with the whole or any part of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:472 | rights and privileges granted under a spectrum right shall take effect
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:473 | until the Authority gives its approval in writing.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:476 | (3) The parties to an assignment of or dealing with the whole or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:477 | any part of the rights and privileges granted under a spectrum right
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:478 | must give to the Authority such information about the assignment or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:479 | dealing as the Authority requires for the purpose of giving its
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:480 | approval under paragraph (2).
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:482 | Variation of conditions of spectrum rights upon assignment
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:483 | 14. The Authority may do any one or more of the following if it is
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:484 | satisfied that it is necessary or convenient to do so in order to give
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:485 | effect to any assignment or dealing under regulation 13:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:486 | (a) vary a spectrum right by changing the name of the person to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:487 | whom the spectrum right was granted;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:488 | (b) vary the conditions of grant of a spectrum right by —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:489 | (i) including one or more further conditions; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:490 | (ii) revoking or varying any condition;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:491 | (c) issue one or more new spectrum rights; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:492 | (d) cancel one or more existing spectrum rights.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:494 | Division 3
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:495 | Variation, suspension, cancellation and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:496 | resumption of Spectrum Rights
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:498 | Variation of certain conditions of spectrum rights
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:499 | 15.—(1) Subject to this regulation, the Authority may vary any
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:500 | condition of any grant of a spectrum right.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:501 | (2) This regulation shall not apply to a resumption of any spectrum
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:502 | right under regulation 17 or 18 or to a variation of the conditions of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:503 | any grant of a spectrum right under regulation 14 or 17 (3).
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:504 | (3) Before varying the conditions of any grant of a spectrum right
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:505 | under this regulation, the Authority shall give notice to the person
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:506 | granted the spectrum right —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:507 | (a) stating that it proposes to make the variations in the manner
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:508 | as specified in the notice; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:509 | (b) specifying the time (not being less than 28 days from the date
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:510 | of service of notice) within which written representations
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:511 | with respect to the proposed variation may be made.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:514 | (4) Upon receipt of any written representation referred to in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:515 | paragraph (3), the Authority shall consider the representation and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:516 | may —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:517 | (a) reject the representation; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:518 | (b) amend the proposed variation in accordance with the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:519 | representation, or in any manner as the Authority considers
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:520 | appropriate,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:521 | and, in either event, the Authority shall issue a direction in writing to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:522 | the person granted the spectrum right requiring that effect be given to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:523 | the proposed variation specified in the notice or to the variation as
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:524 | amended by the Authority within a reasonable time.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:525 | (5) Any person aggrieved by the decision of the Authority under
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:526 | paragraph (4) may, within 14 days of the receipt of the direction,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:527 | appeal to the Minister whose decision shall be final.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:528 | (6) The Authority shall not enforce its direction —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:529 | (a) during the period referred to in paragraph (5); and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:530 | (b) whilst the appeal is under consideration by the Minister.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:531 | (7) If no written representation is received by the Authority within
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:532 | the time specified in paragraph (3) or if any written representation
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:533 | made under that paragraph is subsequently withdrawn, the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:534 | may forthwith carry out the variation as specified in the notice given
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:535 | under that paragraph.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:536 | (8) Notwithstanding paragraphs (3) to (7), the Authority may
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:537 | with the agreement of the person granted the spectrum right vary
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:538 | the conditions of any spectrum right in such manner as may be
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:539 | agreed.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:541 | Suspension or cancellation of spectrum rights
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:542 | 16.—(1) The Authority may suspend or cancel the grant of any
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:543 | spectrum right, or a part of a spectrum right, if the Authority is
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:544 | satisfied that —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:545 | (a) the grant of the spectrum right was obtained by fraud or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:546 | misrepresentation; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:547 | (b) the person to whom the spectrum right is granted, is
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:548 | contravening, or has contravened —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:549 | (i) any of the provisions of the Act or these Regulations;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:552 | (ii) any condition of the grant of the spectrum right; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:553 | (iii) any direction given to the person by the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:554 | under the Act or these Regulations.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:555 | (2) The Authority, before suspending or cancelling the grant of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:556 | any spectrum right, shall give to the person to whom the spectrum
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:557 | right was granted notice in writing of its intention to do so and shall
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:558 | in such notice call upon that person to show cause within such time as
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:559 | may be specified in the notice as to why the person’s spectrum right
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:560 | should not be suspended or cancelled.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:561 | (3) If the person to whom a notice has been given under
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:562 | subsection (2) —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:563 | (a) fails to show cause within the period of time given to him to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:564 | do so or such extended period of time as the Authority may
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:565 | allow; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:566 | (b) fails to show sufficient cause,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:567 | the Authority shall give notice in writing to that person of the date
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:568 | from which the suspension or cancellation of the person’s spectrum
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:569 | right, as the case may be, is to take effect.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:571 | Resumption of spectrum rights by agreement
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:572 | 17.—(1) The Authority may resume a spectrum right, or a part of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:573 | a spectrum right, under an agreement entered into with the person
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:574 | granted the spectrum right.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:575 | (2) Without limiting the matters that may be included in the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:576 | agreement, if a part of the spectrum right is to be resumed, the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:577 | agreement must specify the variations to the other conditions of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:578 | spectrum right that will be made to give effect to the agreement and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:579 | the date on which the resumption is to take effect.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:580 | (3) If a part of the spectrum right is resumed, the Authority shall
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:581 | vary, in a way that gives effect to the variations specified in the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:582 | agreement, the other conditions of the grant of spectrum right.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:583 | (4) For the purposes of this regulation and regulation 18,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:584 | ‘‘resume’’, in relation to a grant of any spectrum right or part of a
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:585 | spectrum right, means to revoke or vary any condition relating to —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:586 | (a) the range of the radio frequencies comprised in the grant of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:587 | the spectrum right;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:590 | (b) the duration of the grant of the spectrum right; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:591 | (c) the geographical area covered by the grant of the spectrum
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:592 | right.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:594 | Resumption of spectrum rights compulsorily
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:595 | 18.—(1) Subject to this regulation, the Authority may resume a
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:596 | spectrum right, or a part of a spectrum right, without the agreement
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:597 | of the person granted the spectrum right.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:598 | (2) The Authority may only resume a spectrum right or a part of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:599 | a spectrum right without agreement of the person granted the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:600 | spectrum right if the Minister has approved the resumption by
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:601 | notification published in the Gazette.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:602 | (3) Before resuming a spectrum right or a part of a spectrum right
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:603 | under this regulation, the Authority shall give notice to the person
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:604 | granted the spectrum right —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:605 | (a) stating that it proposes to resume the spectrum right or a
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:606 | part of the spectrum right in the manner specified in the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:607 | notice and the compensation payable for the resumption;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:608 | (b) specifying the time (not being less than 28 days from the date
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:609 | of service of notice) within which written representations on
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:610 | the proposed resumption may be made; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:611 | (c) if applicable, specifying the variations to the other conditions
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:612 | of the spectrum right that will be made to give effect to the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:613 | resumption.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:614 | (4) Upon receipt of any written representation referred to in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:615 | paragraph (3), the Authority shall consider the representation and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:616 | may —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:617 | (a) reject the representation; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:618 | (b) amend the proposed resumption, the compensation payable
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:619 | and the variations to the other conditions of the spectrum
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:620 | right, in accordance with the representation, or in any other
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:621 | manner as the Authority considers appropriate,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:622 | and, in either event, the Authority shall issue a direction in writing to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:623 | the person granted the spectrum right requiring that effect be given to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:624 | the proposed resumption specified in the notice or to the resumption
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:625 | as subsequently amended by the Authority within a reasonable time.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:628 | (5) Any person aggrieved by the decision of the Authority under
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:629 | paragraph (4) may, within 14 days of the receipt of the direction,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:630 | appeal to the Minister whose decision shall be final.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:631 | (6) The Authority shall not enforce its direction —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:632 | (a) during the period referred to in paragraph (5); and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:633 | (b) whilst the appeal is under consideration by the Minister.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:634 | (7) If no written representation is received by the Authority within
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:635 | the time specified in paragraph (3) or if any written representation
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:636 | made under that paragraph is subsequently withdrawn, the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:637 | may forthwith carry out the resumption as specified in the notice
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:638 | given under that paragraph.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:639 | (8) Regulation 15 shall not apply to the variations to the other
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:640 | conditions of the spectrum right made under this regulation.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:642 | PART IV
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:643 | REQUIREMENT FOR LICENSING
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:645 | Licensing requirement
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:646 | 19.—(1) A station or network may be possessed, established,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:647 | installed, maintained, provided or operated if authorised by —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:648 | (a) a station (spectrum) licence or network (spectrum) licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:649 | (b) a station licence or network licence; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:650 | (c) a class licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:651 | (2) Every application for, and renewal of, a licence shall be made
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:652 | in such form and manner as the Authority may determine and shall be
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:653 | supported by such information as the Authority may require.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:654 | (3) A licence shall be valid for such period as the Authority may
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:655 | determine unless cancelled, suspended or reduced in duration in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:656 | accordance with the provisions of the Act and shall be subject to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:657 | such conditions, restrictions and limitations as the Authority may
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:658 | determine.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:660 | Restrictions on grant of licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:661 | 20. A licence, other than a class licence, shall only be granted by
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:662 | the Authority to —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:663 | (a) a citizen of Singapore;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:666 | (b) a company incorporated under the Companies Act (Cap. 50);
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:667 | (c) a business registered under the Business Registration Act
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:668 | (Cap. 32); or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:669 | (d) such other person as the Authority considers appropriate.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:671 | Licensee not exempted from other laws
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:672 | 21. The grant of any licence referred to in these Regulations does
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:673 | not exempt the licensee from obtaining any other approval, permit,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:674 | licence or other authorisation required by law for or in connection
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:675 | with the possession, establishment, installation, maintenance,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:676 | provision or operation of any station or network.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:678 | Other conditions not affected
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:679 | 22. The conditions of any licence imposed under these Regulations
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:680 | shall be in addition to and not in derogation of any other condition
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:681 | imposed and specified by the Authority in the licence under
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:682 | section 5 of the Act.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:684 | PART V
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:685 | STATION (SPECTRUM) LICENCE AND
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:686 | NETWORK (SPECTRUM) LICENCE
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:688 | Grant of station (spectrum) licence and network (spectrum) licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:689 | 23.—(1) A station (spectrum) licence or a network (spectrum)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:690 | licence may, upon payment of the fees specified in Part I of the First
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:691 | Schedule, be granted by the Authority under section 5 of the Act if
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:692 | the Authority is satisfied that the station or network is to be operated
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:693 | using a spectrum right granted by the Authority and the station or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:694 | network —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:695 | (a) meets with and conforms to applicable —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:696 | (i) emission standards; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:697 | (ii) technical requirements,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:698 | as may be imposed by the Authority; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:699 | (b) is of the kind or class that is approved by the Authority for
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:700 | use under a spectrum right.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:703 | (2) Any station (spectrum) licence and network (spectrum) licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:704 | referred to in paragraph (1) shall specify —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:705 | (a) the conditions of usage of the station or network;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:706 | (b) the duration of the licence; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:707 | (c) such other conditions as the Authority considers appropriate.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:708 | (3) All fees shall be paid in advance and if any fee remains unpaid
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:709 | 7 days after the date on which a station (spectrum) licence or network
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:710 | (spectrum) licence should have been renewed, the following late
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:711 | payment fee shall be charged:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:712 | (a) where the station (spectrum) licence or network (spectrum)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:713 | licence is renewed after 7 days but less than 15 days
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:714 | following the expiration of the previous licence, a sum of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:715 | $10;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:716 | (b) where the station (spectrum) licence or network (spectrum)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:717 | licence is renewed after 14 days but less than 31 days
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:718 | following the expiration of the previous licence, a sum of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:719 | $20; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:720 | (c) where the station (spectrum) licence or network (spectrum)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:721 | licence is renewed after 30 days following the expiration of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:722 | the previous licence, a sum of $50.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:724 | Particulars and records of station (spectrum) licences and network
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:725 | (spectrum) licences
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:726 | 24.—(1) A station or network under a station (spectrum) licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:727 | or network (spectrum) licence shall not be changed or modified in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:728 | respect of any of the particulars mentioned in the licence, including
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:729 | the radio-communication equipment comprised therein, the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:730 | operating radio frequencies and the location at which the station or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:731 | network is installed, except with the prior approval of the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:732 | (2) The licensee shall keep an up-to-date record of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:733 | radio-communication equipment comprised in the station or network.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:734 | (3) The record referred to in paragraph (2) shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:735 | (a) contain such information;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:736 | (b) be kept in such form; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:737 | (c) be submitted to the Authority at such intervals,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:738 | as the Authority may, from time to time, require.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:741 | (4) The licensee shall, at all reasonable times, permit an authorised
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:742 | officer to inspect and make copies of any entry in the record.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:744 | PART VI
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:745 | STATION LICENCE AND NETWORK LICENCE
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:746 | Division 1
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:747 | Grant of, fees for and withdrawal of radio frequency
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:748 | allocated to, station licence and network licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:750 | Grant of station licence and network licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:751 | 25.—(1) The following network licences and station licences may
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:752 | be granted under section 5 of the Act:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:753 | (a) Network Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:754 | (b) Ship Station Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:755 | (c) Aircraft Station Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:756 | (d) Amateur Station Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:757 | (e) Experimental Station Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:758 | (f) Localised Radio-communication Station Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:759 | (g) General Radio-communication Station Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:760 | (h) Satellite Communication Station Licence; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:761 | (i) Special Purpose Station Licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:762 | (2) A station licence or network licence authorises the licensee to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:763 | operate the specified station or network in accordance with the Act,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:764 | these Regulations and the conditions of the licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:765 | (3) The Authority must not grant a station licence or network
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:766 | licence that authorises the operation of a station or network in any
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:767 | radio frequency band that is within a part of the radio frequency
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:768 | spectrum that the Authority has determined under regulation 6 (1) to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:769 | be allocated by the grant of spectrum rights unless the Authority is
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:770 | satisfied that the circumstances of the particular case justify the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:771 | granting of the licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:773 | Fees
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:774 | 26.—(1) The licence fees payable for station licences and network
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:775 | licences are specified in Part II of the First Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:778 | (2) The application and processing fees for use of any radio
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:779 | frequency in the course of operating or using a station or network
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:780 | under a station licence or network licence are specified in Part III of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:781 | the First Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:782 | (3) The annual fees payable for use of any radio frequency in the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:783 | course of operating or using a station or network under a station
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:784 | licence or network licence are specified in Part IV of the First
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:785 | Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:786 | (4) The Authority may, in the interest of spectrum economy and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:787 | after considering the re-usability of a radio frequency, the area of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:788 | coverage involved and the period of use of an assigned radio
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:789 | frequency, reduce the application and processing fees payable under
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:790 | paragraph (2) or the annual fees payable under paragraph (3) or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:791 | both.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:792 | (5) For any multi-channel radio-communication equipment used
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:793 | for transmitting or receiving, the radio frequency fee payable shall be
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:794 | in accordance with the bandwidth of frequencies assigned as specified
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:795 | in Part IV of the First Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:796 | (6) All fees shall be paid in advance and if any fee remains unpaid
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:797 | 7 days after the date on which a station licence or network licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:798 | should have been renewed, the following late payment fee shall be
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:799 | charged:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:800 | (a) where the station licence or network licence is renewed after
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:801 | 7 days but less than 15 days following the expiration of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:802 | previous licence, a sum of $10;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:803 | (b) where the station licence or network licence is renewed after
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:804 | 14 days but less than 31 days following the expiration of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:805 | previous licence, a sum of $20; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:806 | (c) where the station licence or network licence is renewed after
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:807 | 30 days following the expiration of the previous licence, a
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:808 | sum of $50.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:810 | Power of Authority to change or withdraw radio frequency
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:811 | 27. The Authority may, in its discretion and without paying
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:812 | compensation and upon giving such notice as it considers appropriate,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:813 | change or withdraw any radio frequency allocated to the licensee
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:814 | under the station licence or network licence without assigning any
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:815 | reason therefor.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:818 | Division 2
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:819 | Types of Station Licence and Network Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:820 | Network Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:822 | Network Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:823 | 28.—(1) The Authority may grant the following classes of Network
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:824 | Licences:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:825 | (a) Localised Private Network Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:826 | (b) Wide-area Private Network Licence; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:827 | (c) Public Mobile Network Licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:828 | (2) The grant of a private network licence shall not, unless the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:829 | Authority otherwise determines, authorise the licensee to provide,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:830 | directly or indirectly, any telecommunication service to the general
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:831 | public.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:832 | (3) A Network Licence shall only be granted in respect of a
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:833 | network that meets all technical standards and any other
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:834 | requirements which the Authority may, from time to time, stipulate.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:835 | (4) The Authority may refuse to grant a Localised Private
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:836 | Network Licence or Wide-area Private Network Licence if it is
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:837 | satisfied that —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:838 | (a) the licensee failed to meet the minimum channel loading
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:839 | criteria set by the Authority from time to time for the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:840 | network; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:841 | (b) the radio-communication service that is, or is intended to be,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:842 | provided by or through the network may be adequately
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:843 | provided by or through a public telecommunication system
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:844 | or by any other means.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:846 | Ship Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:848 | Ship Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:849 | 29.—(1) A Ship Station Licence may be granted by the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:850 | if —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:851 | (a) the ship on which the station is to be carried (referred to in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:852 | this regulation as the ship) has a valid internationally
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:853 | recognised Safety Radio certificate;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:856 | (b) the station is operated by an appropriate number and category
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:857 | of radio operators holding a Certificate of Competency
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:858 | granted under the Radio-communication (Certificates of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:859 | Competency for Ship Station Operators) Regulations (Rg 2)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:860 | or a competent foreign authority recognised by the Authority,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:861 | except where the vessel is used solely or principally for
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:862 | pleasure purposes;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:863 | (c) the ship has an accounting authority acceptable to the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:864 | Authority; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:865 | (d) the ship complies with such other requirements as may be
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:866 | determined by the Authority from time to time.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:867 | (2) A person who is unable to furnish all the information required
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:868 | by the Authority in the application form for a Ship Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:869 | may, upon payment of the prescribed fee and upon satisfying such
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:870 | other requirements as may be determined by the Authority, be
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:871 | granted a Provisional Ship Station Licence which shall be valid for
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:872 | such period and subject to such conditions as may be determined by
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:873 | the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:875 | Restrictions on grant of Ship Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:876 | 30. A Ship Station Licence shall only be granted in respect of a
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:877 | ship, including its lifeboats, which is registered or licensed by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:878 | competent authority in Singapore.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:880 | Compliance with Radio Regulations, Authority’s requirements, etc.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:881 | 31. A Ship Station licensee shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:882 | (a) provide on board the ship all documents either considered
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:883 | necessary by the Authority or required under the Radio
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:884 | Regulations for the efficient operation of the station carried
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:885 | on board the ship; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:886 | (b) comply with the working procedures set out in the Radio
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:887 | Regulations and with such other requirements as the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:888 | Authority may determine.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:890 | Equipment not to cause interference
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:891 | 32.—(1) A station on board any ship in the waters of Singapore
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:892 | shall be operated in such manner as not to impair or interfere with —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:893 | (a) any Armed Forces Communication; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:896 | (b) the efficient and convenient working of any other station or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:897 | network, or telecommunication system or service in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:898 | Singapore authorised by the Authority under the Act or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:899 | these Regulations.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:900 | (2) A station on board any ship must not be used if the crew of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:901 | the ship observes, or when the crew has been informed by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:902 | Authority, that the working of the station causes interference to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:903 | radio-communication.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:905 | Restrictions on use of equipment while in territorial waters
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:906 | 33.—(1) Subject to paragraph (2), no station on board a ship
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:907 | shall be used while the ship is within the territorial waters of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:908 | Singapore.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:909 | (2) A station on board a ship, whether licensed by the Authority or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:910 | by a foreign competent authority, may be used while the ship is within
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:911 | the territorial waters of Singapore for the purposes of —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:912 | (a) safety of navigation, life or property or for any other
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:913 | purposes as may be authorised by the Authority; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:914 | (b) communication on such radio frequency bands as may be
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:915 | specifically authorised by the Authority, subject to such
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:916 | conditions as may be determined by the Authority, where
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:917 | the use of the station does not cause interference to the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:918 | working of any other station or network licensed under these
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:919 | Regulations.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:921 | Aircraft Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:923 | Restrictions on grant of Aircraft Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:924 | 34. An Aircraft Station Licence shall only be granted in respect of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:925 | a station on a commercial or privately-owned aircraft registered in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:926 | Singapore.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:928 | Duty of licensee in respect of equipment, Radio Regulations, etc.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:929 | 35.—(1) All equipment comprised in a station on board any
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:930 | aircraft must be approved by the Director-General of the Civil
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:931 | Aviation Authority of Singapore and a certificate to this effect shall
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:932 | accompany the application for the licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:935 | (2) An Aircraft Station licensee shall observe the provisions of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:936 | Radio Regulations and any other local or international rules and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:937 | regulations applicable to stations on board an aircraft.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:939 | Restrictions on use of aircraft station
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:940 | 36. No station fitted in an aircraft shall be operated or used while
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:941 | such aircraft is at rest on land or on water in Singapore except —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:942 | (a) in exceptional cases or in time of emergency or distress;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:943 | (b) if communication by means of a telecommunication line
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:944 | system is not available, for communication in exceptional
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:945 | circumstances on matters relating to air navigation and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:946 | services with the nearest aeronautical station, or, if
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:947 | communication with such station is impracticable, with any
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:948 | other station;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:949 | (c) for the purpose of carrying out experimental tests with the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:950 | written approval of and subject to such conditions as may be
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:951 | determined by the Authority; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:952 | (d) for the purpose of carrying out functional tests on
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:953 | frequencies other than on international distress frequencies
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:954 | to determine the serviceability of the station.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:956 | Amateur Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:958 | Amateur Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:959 | 37.—(1) The Authority may grant the following classes of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:960 | Amateur Station Licences to qualified or approved persons
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:961 | interested in the operation of radio-communication equipment solely
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:962 | for pleasure and for the furtherance of radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:963 | techniques and not for pecuniary gain:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:964 | (a) General Class;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:965 | (b) Restricted Class; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:966 | (c) any other class of licence which the Authority considers
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:967 | appropriate.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:968 | (2) Notwithstanding regulation 20, an Amateur Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:969 | may only be granted to a natural person and shall not authorise the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:970 | use of radio-communication equipment by the licensee’s employees.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:973 | Age restrictions
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:974 | 38.—(1) An Amateur Station Licence shall not be granted to a
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:975 | person below the age of 16 years.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:976 | (2) Any application for an Amateur Station Licence by an
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:977 | applicant below the age of 21 years shall be countersigned by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:978 | applicant’s parent, guardian or by any other person approved by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:979 | Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:980 | (3) It is a condition of every Amateur Station Licence that a
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:981 | licensee between the ages of 16 and 21 years may only operate or use
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:982 | any Amateur Station if supervised by a qualified person approved by
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:983 | the Authority and who has agreed to supervise the licensee, and that
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:984 | qualified person shall ensure that the licensee observes and complies
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:985 | with all the duties and obligations specified in the licence and in these
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:986 | Regulations.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:988 | Qualifications
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:989 | 39.—(1) An applicant for an Amateur Station Licence shall, unless
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:990 | exempted by the Authority —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:991 | (a) have passed the Radio Amateur Examination set by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:992 | Authority; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:993 | (b) be in possession of an Amateur Radio Certificate acceptable
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:994 | to the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:995 | (2) The fees payable to sit for the Radio Amateur Examination
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:996 | referred to in paragraph (1) are specified in the Second Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:998 | General conditions
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:999 | 40. An Amateur Station licensee shall observe the following
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1000 | conditions:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1001 | (a) the station shall only be operated at locations approved by
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1002 | the Authority;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1003 | (b) the station shall in all cases be operated by the licensee or by
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1004 | persons named in the licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1005 | (c) the station and all equipment used or intended to be used by
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1006 | the licensee shall be erected, fixed, placed and used, so as not
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1007 | to cause interference to radio-communications in Singapore;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1010 | (d) the licensee shall identify himself by the transmission of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1011 | callsign assigned to him by the Authority at the beginning
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1012 | and end of each transmission;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1013 | (e) any change in the approved location, equipment, mast or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1014 | antenna system must be approved by the Authority prior to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1015 | the change being made;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1016 | (f) the licensee shall obtain the approval of all relevant
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1017 | authorities before erecting any mast or antenna to be used in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1018 | connection with the operation of the station; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1019 | (g) the licensee shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1020 | (i) keep a running record of all transmission periods
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1021 | showing the date and time of each period of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1022 | transmission and the radio frequency and type of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1023 | emission employed;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1024 | (ii) preserve the record of each entry made for one year;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1025 | and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1026 | (iii) make the record mentioned in sub-paragraph (ii)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1027 | available for inspection at all reasonable times by an
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1028 | authorised officer.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1030 | Prohibition on use of encryption devices
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1031 | 41. It is a condition of every Amateur Station Licence that the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1032 | licensee may not make use of encryption devices or equipment in the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1033 | operation or use of any station.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1035 | Restrictions on transmission
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1036 | 42. It is a condition of every Amateur Station Licence that —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1037 | (a) messages transmitted through an Amateur Station shall be
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1038 | in plain language and shall relate solely to the licensee’s
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1039 | experiments or personal affairs (not being business affairs),
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1040 | or to the personal affairs of the person with whom the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1041 | licensee is communicating;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1042 | (b) the Amateur Station shall not be used for transmitting news,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1043 | advertisements, communications of a business or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1044 | non-experimental character, messages for pecuniary reward
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1045 | or messages for or on behalf of a third party;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1048 | (c) except with the written permission of the Authority, no
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1049 | licensee of an Amateur Station shall call or transmit to any
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1050 | station other than an Amateur Station;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1051 | (d) messages may only be exchanged with another Amateur
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1052 | Station, except where prohibited by law; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1053 | (e) transmission shall not commence without listening in on the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1054 | radio frequency to be used in order to ascertain that no
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1055 | interference is likely to be caused to any other station which
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1056 | may be functioning.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1058 | Power of Authority to order transmission
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1059 | 43. It is a condition of every Amateur Station Licence that the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1060 | licensee shall, if required by the Authority by notice in writing,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1061 | transmit any message provided by the Authority by means of his
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1062 | licensed Amateur Station.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1064 | Portable stations
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1065 | 44. The Authority may approve an Amateur Station as a portable
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1066 | or mobile station, subject to such conditions as the Authority may
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1067 | impose.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1069 | Experimental Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1071 | Experimental Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1072 | 45. The Authority may grant an Experimental Station Licence —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1073 | (a) to such educational institutions, training establishments or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1074 | qualified persons as the Authority may determine for the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1075 | purpose of conducting research and development activities,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1076 | experiments or demonstrations in radio-communication; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1077 | (b) to licensed dealers in, or manufacturers or importers of,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1078 | radio-communication equipment for the purpose of testing,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1079 | demonstration or conducting research and development in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1080 | radio-communication equipment.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1082 | Power limitations
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1083 | 46. The Authority may limit the maximum power of a station in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1084 | respect of which an Experimental Station Licence has been granted,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1085 | having regard to the purpose for which the station has been
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1086 | authorised and the conditions under which it is to work.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1089 | Localised Radio-communication Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1091 | Localised Radio-communication Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1092 | 47. The Authority may grant a Localised Radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1093 | Station Licence to approved applicants to use the following equipment:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1094 | (a) remote control devices;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1095 | (b) local area paging devices;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1096 | (c) wireless microphones;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1097 | (d) transceivers (CB walkie talkies);
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1098 | (e) telemetry or alarm systems or both;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1099 | (f) wireless data or voice systems;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1100 | (g) cordless telephones; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1101 | (h) any other radio-communication equipment as may be
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1102 | authorised by the Authority from time to time.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1104 | Sharing of radio frequencies
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1105 | 48.—(1) The radio frequencies allocated to any Localised
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1106 | Radio-communication Station may be shared by other users and the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1107 | Authority shall not be responsible or liable for any interference
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1108 | arising from such use.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1109 | (2) Licensees operating on shared radio frequencies shall accept
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1110 | any interference that may result from the legitimate operation of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1111 | stations, including the operation of industrial, scientific and medical
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1112 | (I.S.M.) equipment, functioning in the I.S.M. Band.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1114 | General Radio-communication Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1116 | General Radio-communication Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1117 | 49. The Authority may grant a General Radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1118 | Station Licence to approved applicants for the purpose of enabling
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1119 | them to transmit, receive or transmit and receive messages by means
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1120 | of radio-communication.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1122 | Common base station and shared radio frequencies
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1123 | 50. It is a condition of every General Radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1124 | Station Licence that the licensee shall, if required by the Authority in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1125 | the interest of radio frequency spectrum economy or for any other
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1128 | reason, work with a common base station operated or licensed by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1129 | Authority or to share a radio frequency with other stations, subject to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1130 | any condition which the Authority may impose.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1132 | Navigation or detection of objects
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1133 | 51. The Authority may grant a General Radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1134 | Station Licence to an approved applicant for the purpose of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1135 | navigating or detecting objects by means of radio-communication.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1137 | Satellite Communication Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1139 | Satellite Communication Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1140 | 52. The Authority may grant the following classes of Satellite
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1141 | Communication Station Licences to enable the licensee to transmit,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1142 | receive or transmit and receive messages by means of satellite
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1143 | communication for such purposes as may be authorised by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1144 | Authority:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1145 | (a) Very Small Aperture Terminal (VSAT) Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1146 | (b) Tracking, Telemetry and Command (TT&C) Earth Station
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1147 | Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1148 | (c) Earth Station Licence; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1149 | (d) Portable Satellite Communication Terminal Licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1151 | Obligations of licensee
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1152 | 53. It is a condition of every Satellite Communication Station
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1153 | Licence that the licensee —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1154 | (a) must seek the approval of the Authority for access to any
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1155 | space segment and shall comply with the relevant rules,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1156 | regulations and procedures imposed by the satellite operator
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1157 | for station access, booking and fees;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1158 | (b) may only use or work within the radio frequencies or radio
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1159 | frequency bands approved by the Authority for his or its use;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1160 | and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1161 | (c) must not, without the written approval of the Authority, use
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1162 | any satellite communication equipment in respect of which
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1163 | the Satellite Communication Station Licence has been issued
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1164 | to provide telecommunication services to the public.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1167 | Compliance with International Telecommunication Convention
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1168 | 54. Unless exempted by the Authority, a Satellite Communication
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1169 | Station licensee shall at all times comply with the provisions of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1170 | the International Telecommunication Convention Station and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1171 | all regulations and recommendations annexed thereto or made
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1172 | thereunder as are applicable to Singapore.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1174 | Special Purpose Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1176 | Special Purpose Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1177 | 55.—(1) The Authority may grant a Special Purpose Station
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1178 | Licence for the installation and operation of any special purpose
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1179 | station.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1180 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1), a ‘‘special purpose station’’
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1181 | is a station not otherwise defined in these Regulations that is
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1182 | established exclusively for such purpose and upon such conditions as
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1183 | the Authority may specify.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1185 | Division 3
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1186 | Specific Provisions Applicable to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1187 | Station Licence and Network Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1189 | Equipment in stations or networks
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1190 | 56.—(1) The Authority may, in respect of any individual or class of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1191 | station licence or network licence, specify the type of equipment that
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1192 | the licensee is authorised to use and, if applicable, the type of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1193 | equipment to be comprised in the individual or class of station or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1194 | network.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1195 | (2) A station or network under a station licence or a network
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1196 | licence shall not be changed or modified in respect of any of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1197 | particulars mentioned in the station licence or network licence,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1198 | including the radio-communication equipment comprised therein, the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1199 | operating radio frequencies and the location at which the station or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1200 | network is installed, except with the prior approval of the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1202 | Records
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1203 | 57.—(1) A licensee of a network shall keep an up-to-date record of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1204 | the radio-communication equipment comprised in the network.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1207 | (2) The record referred to in paragraph (1) shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1208 | (a) contain such information;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1209 | (b) be kept in such form; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1210 | (c) be submitted to the Authority at such intervals,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1211 | as the Authority may, from time to time, require.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1212 | (3) The licensee shall, at all reasonable times, permit an authorised
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1213 | officer to inspect and make copies of any entry in the record.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1215 | Technical requirements
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1216 | 58.—(1) Before a station licence or network licence is granted, the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1217 | applicant shall satisfy the Authority that the station or network in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1218 | respect of which the licence is to be granted conforms to such
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1219 | technical requirements as may be imposed by the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1220 | (2) All equipment comprised in a station licence or network
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1221 | licence shall be approved by the Authority before use.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1222 | (3) Every station or network in respect of which an application for
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1223 | a station licence or network licence has been made or for which a
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1224 | station licence or network licence has been granted may at any time
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1225 | be inspected and tested by an authorised officer.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1227 | PART VII
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1228 | PROVISIONS APPLICABLE TO
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1229 | STATION (SPECTRUM) LICENCES,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1230 | NETWORK (SPECTRUM) LICENCES,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1231 | STATION LICENCES AND NETWORK LICENCES
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1233 | Modification of conditions
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1234 | 59. Subject to section 7 of the Act, where the Authority modifies
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1235 | all or any of the conditions upon which a station (spectrum) licence,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1236 | network (spectrum) licence, station licence or network licence is
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1237 | granted or imposes any additional conditions, the licensee shall, at its
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1238 | own expense, comply with the modified or additional conditions.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1240 | Assignment, transfer, etc., of benefits of licence only with approval
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1241 | 60.—(1) Except with the approval in writing of the Authority, a
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1242 | licensee shall not assign, transfer, sublet or otherwise dispose of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1243 | benefit of any station (spectrum) licence, network (spectrum) licence,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1246 | station licence or network licence granted under these Regulations,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1247 | or permit another person to participate in any of the benefits, powers
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1248 | or authority granted under such licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1249 | (2) It is a condition of every station (spectrum) licence, network
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1250 | (spectrum) licence, station licence and network licence that every
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1251 | station and network under the licence must be under the control of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1252 | the licensee unless the Authority otherwise permits in writing.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1254 | Employees of licensee
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1255 | 61. It is a condition of every station (spectrum) licence, network
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1256 | (spectrum) licence, station licence and network licence that the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1257 | licensee shall ensure that his or its employees comply with the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1258 | provisions of the Act, these Regulations and the conditions of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1259 | licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1261 | Amendment of licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1262 | 62.—(1) Amendments to a station (spectrum) licence, network
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1263 | (spectrum) licence, station licence or network licence for —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1264 | (a) the transfer of location of a station other than the transfer of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1265 | a portable or mobile station from one site to another; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1266 | (b) any change in the radio-communication equipment comprised
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1267 | in the station,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1268 | may only be made if the station has been satisfactorily inspected by an
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1269 | authorised officer and the Authority has approved the transfer or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1270 | change.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1271 | (2) Where an authorised officer inspects a station under
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1272 | paragraph (1), the Authority may impose a fee of $150 for the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1273 | inspection.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1274 | (3) Any amendment to a station (spectrum) licence, network
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1275 | (spectrum) licence, station licence or network licence for a
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1276 | change in the base or repeater station in the network may only
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1277 | be made if —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1278 | (a) the licensee has notified the Authority of the change;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1279 | (b) the base or repeater station has been inspected to the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1280 | satisfaction of an authorised officer; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1281 | (c) the Authority approves the change.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1284 | Return of licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1285 | 63.—(1) When a licensee ceases to operate a station or network
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1286 | or when a station (spectrum) licence, network (spectrum) licence,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1287 | station licence or network licence ceases to be valid, the licensee
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1288 | shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1289 | (a) return the licence to the Authority for cancellation; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1290 | (b) if required by the Authority, seal, disable or dismantle the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1291 | radio-communication equipment comprised in the station or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1292 | network in the presence of any authorised officer.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1293 | (2) Unless authorised by the Authority, the licensee may only
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1294 | dispose of or offer the station, network or any radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1295 | equipment comprised therein for sale if it has first been sealed,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1296 | disabled or dismantled.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1297 | (3) Where any radio-communication equipment has been sealed,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1298 | disabled or dismantled under paragraph (1), no person shall, unless
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1299 | authorised by the Authority, break or tamper with the seal or enable
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1300 | or reassemble the equipment, as the case may be.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1301 | (4) Where a station (spectrum) licence, network (spectrum)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1302 | licence, station licence or network licence is returned to the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1303 | Authority, no compensation shall be paid by the Authority to the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1304 | licensee and no fee or part thereof shall, unless provided for in the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1305 | licence, be refunded by the Authority to the licensee in respect of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1306 | unexpired period of such licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1308 | Notification of change of particulars
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1309 | 64. A station (spectrum) licensee, network (spectrum) licensee,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1310 | station licensee or network licensee, as the case may be, shall notify
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1311 | the Authority of any change in its particulars specified in a licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1312 | within 14 days of the change.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1314 | PART VIII
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1315 | CLASS LICENCES
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1317 | Grant of class licences
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1318 | 65.—(1) A person who possesses or uses a relevant radio-
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1319 | communication station shall be deemed to have been granted a class
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1320 | licence by the Authority for that purpose.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1323 | (2) A class licence shall be subject to the conditions specified in the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1324 | Third Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1325 | (3) No fee is payable for a class licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1326 | (4) For the purposes of this regulation and the Third Schedule,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1327 | ‘‘relevant radio-communication station’’ means a radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1328 | station that is connected with any of the following telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1329 | systems licensed under section 5 of the Act:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1330 | (a) a public cellular mobile telephone system;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1331 | (b) a public radio paging system;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1332 | (c) a public mobile data system;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1333 | (d) a public trunked radio system;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1334 | (e) a public satellite mobile telephone or data system,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1335 | and includes a radio-communication station that is capable of being
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1336 | used in connection with any of the telecommunication systems
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1337 | referred to in sub-paragraphs (a) to (e) but which is not in use and not
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1338 | so connected.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1340 | PART IX
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1341 | DUTIES AND GENERAL OBLIGATIONS
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1343 | Inspection of radio-communication equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1344 | 66.—(1) It is a condition of every licence that the licensee shall
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1345 | permit or ensure that permission is granted to an authorised officer,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1346 | upon production of proof of identity, to enter any building, premises,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1347 | compound or other place, vehicle, vessel or aircraft where any station
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1348 | or network is installed, or is being installed, to enable that officer to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1349 | inspect, examine or test any equipment comprised in the station or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1350 | network.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1351 | (2) Where the owner or user of a station or network requests the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1352 | Authority to inspect, for the second or subsequent time, any station
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1353 | or network licensed or to be licensed under these Regulations to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1354 | verify that the station or network or any equipment comprised
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1355 | therein is designed, constructed, installed, established, maintained or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1356 | operated in accordance with any of the provisions of the Act, these
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1357 | Regulations or any condition of the licence, the Authority may
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1358 | impose a fee of $150 for the inspection.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1361 | Inspection of licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1362 | 67. A licensee of a station or network shall permit an authorised
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1363 | officer or a police officer not below the rank of sergeant, upon
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1364 | production of proof of identity, to examine his or its licence, or if it is
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1365 | not immediately available, produce the licence at the office of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1366 | Authority or a police station named by the police officer within a
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1367 | reasonable period.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1369 | Secrecy
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1370 | 68.—(1) Except as may be provided by section 42 (2) of the Act,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1371 | no person shall intercept or acquaint himself with the contents of any
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1372 | radio-communication other than those transmitted for general
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1373 | information or for the information of licensees belonging to the same
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1374 | licensed network.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1375 | (2) Except as otherwise provided in these Regulations or by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1376 | conditions of a licence granted under these Regulations, every person
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1377 | having access to radio-communications shall hold strictly secret all
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1378 | radio-communications, other than those transmitted for general
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1379 | information, which may pass through his hands or come to his
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1380 | knowledge.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1381 | (3) Every person referred to in paragraph (2) shall not —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1382 | (a) directly or indirectly, disclose the contents of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1383 | radio-communications referred to in that paragraph except
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1384 | to a person entitled to become acquainted with the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1385 | radio-communications or to an authorised officer or to a
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1386 | court; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1387 | (b) make any other use of such radio-communications.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1388 | (4) No person having unauthorised access to radio-communications
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1389 | shall print or publish or cause to be printed or published in any
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1390 | newspaper, pamphlet, book or document, any radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1391 | that may pass through his hands or come to his knowledge, whether
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1392 | such radio-communication is for private or general reception.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1394 | Station and network to be used for lawful purposes
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1395 | 69. No person shall operate or use any station or network for or in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1396 | furtherance of any unlawful purpose.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1399 | Restrictions on transmission
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1400 | 70.—(1) The transmission of superfluous signals by a station or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1401 | network is prohibited.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1402 | (2) No test, trial or practical transmission shall be permitted except
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1403 | in such circumstances as to preclude the possibility of interference
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1404 | with any other station or network.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1405 | (3) All tests, unless prior approval from the Authority has been
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1406 | obtained, shall be conducted on dummy load.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1407 | (4) No person shall transmit —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1408 | (a) any message containing indecent, obscene or offensive
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1409 | language;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1410 | (b) any message for an improper or illegal purpose;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1411 | (c) any message which interferes with the operation of any
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1412 | authorised station or network; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1413 | (d) any message which, to his knowledge, is false or misleading
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1414 | and likely to prejudice the efficiency of any life-service or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1415 | endanger the safety of any person or of a place or premises,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1416 | vessel, aircraft or vehicle.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1417 | (5) A licensee shall ensure that his or its station or network is
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1418 | worked in a manner which is safe and which does not impair or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1419 | interfere with —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1420 | (a) any Armed Forces Communication; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1421 | (b) the efficient and convenient working or maintenance of any
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1422 | other station or network, or telecommunication system or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1423 | service in Singapore authorised by the Authority under the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1424 | Act or these Regulations.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1425 | (6) A licensee shall cease operating his or its station or network
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1426 | and shall take any other immediate action which the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1427 | stipulates as soon as the licensee observes, or when the licensee has
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1428 | been informed by the Authority or any other competent authority,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1429 | that the working of the station or network causes interference to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1430 | radio-communication.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1431 | (7) The licensee shall, where so directed by the Authority in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1432 | writing, cease to operate all or any of the equipment comprised in his
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1433 | or its station for such period or periods of time as may be required by
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1434 | the Authority for the purposes of investigation of interference to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1435 | radio-communications.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1438 | International Telecommunication Convention
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1439 | 71.—(1) The provisions of the International Telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1440 | Convention and the regulations for the time being in force thereunder
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1441 | shall, so far as they are applicable, apply to any station or network
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1442 | established or operated in Singapore and to any message transmitted
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1443 | or received by such station or network.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1444 | (2) The Authority may, in its discretion, waive the application of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1445 | any of the provisions or regulations referred to in paragraph (1) to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1446 | any station, network or message.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1448 | Inspection to determine cause of interference
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1449 | 72. It is a condition of every licence that any owner or user of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1450 | electrical, electronic or radio-communication equipment under the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1451 | licence causing or suspected of causing electrical or radiated
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1452 | interference or disturbance to telecommunication equipment,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1453 | stations, networks or systems belonging to or authorised or approved
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1454 | by the Authority shall permit an authorised officer to inspect his or its
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1455 | equipment in order to determine whether the interference is in fact
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1456 | caused by the equipment.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1458 | Investigation by Authority upon request
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1459 | 73.—(1) The Authority may, where requested by any person to —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1460 | (a) investigate, for the second or subsequent time, the cause
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1461 | of electrical or radiated interference or disturbance to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1462 | telecommunication equipment, stations, networks or systems;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1463 | or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1464 | (b) measure and compute the field strength of radiated
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1465 | electromagnetic energy of any electrical, electronic or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1466 | radio-communication equipment,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1467 | charge a fee of $100 per hour or part thereof for work done.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1468 | (2) Where the Authority undertakes to measure and compute
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1469 | the field strength of radiated electromagnetic energy under
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1470 | paragraph (1), the Authority shall determine the measuring device
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1471 | to be used, the method by which and the conditions under which
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1472 | tests are to be conducted and the manner in which the field
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1473 | strength from readings afforded by the measuring device is
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1474 | computed.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1477 | Instructions to eliminate or reduce interference
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1478 | 74.—(1) Where the Authority determines that interference or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1479 | disturbance to telecommunication equipment, stations, networks or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1480 | systems is or may be caused by any particular electrical, electronic or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1481 | radio-communication equipment, the Authority may, by notice in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1482 | writing, direct the owner or user of that electrical, electronic or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1483 | radio-communication equipment to do, at his or its own expense, any
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1484 | one or more of the following:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1485 | (a) take suitable measures to eliminate or reduce the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1486 | interference or disturbance;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1487 | (b) remedy a fault in or the improper operation of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1488 | equipment;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1489 | (c) modify or alter the equipment; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1490 | (d) disconnect the equipment.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1491 | (2) The Authority may require any action required to be taken
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1492 | under paragraph (1) to be effected within such period of time as the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1493 | Authority may determine having regard to the circumstances of each
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1494 | case.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1495 | (3) In addition to any action the Authority may take under this
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1496 | regulation, the Authority may —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1497 | (a) by notice in writing, prohibit the installation or use of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1498 | that equipment unless and until the directions under
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1499 | paragraphs (1) and (2) are complied with; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1500 | (b) where it considers it necessary, seal or remove the electrical,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1501 | electronic or radio-communication equipment or any part
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1502 | thereof referred to in paragraph (1).
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1504 | Fees for ad hoc temporary radio frequency assignment
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1505 | 75.—(1) The Authority may permit any person to use any radio
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1506 | frequency band in respect of any network or station for a period
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1507 | not exceeding 90 days at a time upon payment of the fees specified
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1508 | in Part V of the First Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1509 | (2) Paragraph (1) shall not apply to any use of radio frequency
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1510 | band granted under a spectrum right, or permitted under a station
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1511 | (spectrum) licence, a network (spectrum) licence, a station licence, a
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1512 | network licence or a class licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1515 | PART X
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1516 | MISCELLANEOUS
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1518 | Application of Telecom Competition Code
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1519 | 76. No approval, consent, licence or authorisation given by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1520 | Authority pursuant to these Regulations shall be taken as specifically
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1521 | authorising or approving any act or thing for the purposes of the Code
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1522 | of Practice for Competition in the provision of Telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1523 | Services issued by the Authority under section 26 of the Act.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1525 | Replacement licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1526 | 77.—(1) If the Authority is satisfied that any licence issued by it is
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1527 | lost, destroyed or defaced, the Authority may, upon payment of a fee
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1528 | of $10, issue a replacement licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1529 | (2) No replacement licence shall be issued in place of a defaced
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1530 | licence unless the defaced licence is surrendered to the Authority for
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1531 | cancellation.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1533 | Offence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1534 | 78. Any person who —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1535 | (a) contravenes regulation 24, 31, 32, 33, 35 (2), 36, 54, 56 (2), 57,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1536 | 63 (1), (2) or (3), 64, 67, 68, 69 or 70; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1537 | (b) contravenes any direction or notice of the Authority issued
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1538 | under regulation 74,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1539 | shall be guilty of an offence.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1541 | Waiver
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1542 | 79. The Minister or the Authority (subject to the directions of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1543 | Minister) may waive the application of all or any of the provisions of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1544 | these Regulations, any or all of the conditions in any licence and any
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1545 | fee payable under these Regulations.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1547 | Revocation, savings and transitional provisions
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1548 | 80.—(1) The Radio-communication Regulations (Cap. 323, Rg 3)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1549 | are revoked.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1552 | (2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), the holder of any licence in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1553 | respect of any network or station granted in accordance with the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1554 | revoked Radio-communication Regulations may —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1555 | (a) until the expiry of the licence or unless the licence is
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1556 | cancelled or suspended in accordance with the Act; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1557 | (b) subject to the provisions of the revoked Radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1558 | Regulations,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1559 | perform all the acts for which the licence was granted as if these
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1560 | Regulations had not been enacted.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1562 | FIRST SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1563 | Regulations 23 (1), 26 (1),
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1564 | (2), (3) and (5) and 75 (1)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1566 | PART I
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1567 | FEES FOR STATION (SPECTRUM) LICENCE AND
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1568 | NETWORK (SPECTRUM) LICENCE
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1571 | First column Second column
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1572 | Types of licences Fee payable per annum
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1574 | 1. General Radio-communication Station —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1575 | (a) Base or Fixed Station $100
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1576 | (b) Mobile Station $50
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1577 | (c) Fixed Link or Relay Station $100
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1579 | 2. Wide-area Private Network —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1580 | (a) Portable or Mobile Station $500 per group of 50 stations
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1581 | or part thereof
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1582 | (b) Base or Repeater Station $100
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1584 | 3. Public Mobile Network —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1585 | (a) 300 Base Stations or less $100 per station
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1586 | (b) 301 to 500 Base Stations $80 per station for all stations
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1587 | (c) 501 to 700 Base Stations $60 per station for all stations
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1588 | (d) 701 Base Stations or more $40 per station for all stations
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1590 | 4. Fixed Wireless Broadband Network $500 per group of 50 stations
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1591 | or part thereof.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1594 | FIRST SCHEDULE — continued
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1596 | PART II
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1597 | FEES FOR STATION LICENCE AND NETWORK LICENCE
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1599 | First column Second column
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1600 | Types of licences Fee payable per annum
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1602 | 1. Ship Station $50
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1604 | 2. Aircraft Station $50
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1606 | 3. Amateur Station —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1607 | (a) General Class $50
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1608 | (b) Restricted Class $25
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1610 | 4. Experimental Station $50
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1612 | 5. Localised Radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1613 | Station —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1614 | (a) Remote Control Devices (i) $25 (Personal use)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1615 | (aircraft models and cranes) (ii) $50 (Business use)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1616 | (b) Local Area Paging Devices Base $50
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1617 | Station
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1618 | (c) Wireless Microphones (i) $25 (Personal use)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1619 | (ii) $50 (Business use)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1620 | (d) Transceivers (CB Walkie Talkies) (i) $25 (Personal use)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1621 | (ii) $50 (Business use)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1622 | (e) Telemetry or Alarm Systems or $50
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1623 | both
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1624 | (f) Wireless Data or Voice Systems (i) $50 for 50 stations or less
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1625 | (ii) $100 for more than 50
