-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1790 | Regulation 65 (2) and (4)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1792 | CONDITIONS OF CLASS LICENCE
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1794 | 1. A class licensee shall comply with the technical specifications laid down
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1795 | from time to time by the Authority in relation to the relevant radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1796 | station.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1798 | 2. A class licensee shall ensure that the relevant radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1799 | station is approved by the Authority before it is used for connection to any
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1800 | telecommunication system or equipment belonging to a public telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1801 | licensee, and that the relevant radio-communication station is not tampered with or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1802 | modified in any manner after the approval of the Authority has been obtained.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1804 | 3. A class licensee shall ensure that the relevant radio-communication station
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1805 | is not used for any unlawful purpose.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1807 | 4. The Authority may cancel or suspend a class licence if it is satisfied that the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1808 | class licensee is contravening, or has contravened and is likely again to contravene,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1809 | any of these conditions or the provisions of the Act or any regulations made
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1810 | thereunder.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1813 | Made this 28th day of February 2001.
